<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  This project currently signs with a FREE Apple Developer Personal Team.

  Two capabilities are therefore unavailable, and adding their keys here
  will fail code signing rather than enable the feature:

    1. Push notifications      (aps-environment)
    2. Universal links         (com.apple.developer.associated-domains)

  Consequences today:
    - Remote/push notifications do not arrive. NotificationService detects
      the missing APNs token and skips device registration quietly.
      In-app polling still surfaces new messages.
    - https://kanairoxo.online/... links open Safari, not the app.
      The kanairoxo:// custom scheme DOES work on a free team and routes
      through DeepLinks — that path is unaffected.

  ── When upgrading to a paid membership ($99/yr) ────────────────────────
  Add both keys back:

    <key>aps-environment</key>
    <string>development</string>

    <key>com.apple.developer.associated-domains</key>
    <array>
      <string>applinks:kanairoxo.online</string>
      <string>applinks:app.kanairoxo.online</string>
    </array>

  Then also:
    - Enable Push Notifications + Associated Domains on the App ID in the
      Apple Developer portal.
    - Upload the APNs auth key (.p8) to Firebase Console → Project
      Settings → Cloud Messaging. Without it FCM cannot deliver to iOS
      even once the entitlement is present.
    - Serve /.well-known/apple-app-site-association from both domains
      over HTTPS, no redirect, Content-Type application/json.
    - Switch aps-environment to "production" for TestFlight/App Store.

  The app-group below powers the home-screen widget and works on free
  accounts — leave it in place.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>com.apple.security.application-groups</key>
    <array>
        <string>group.com.kanairoxo.kanairoxo</string>
    </array>
</dict>
</plist>
